AB  - Rival Civilisations: The Rise of Japan and Visions of World Order in Britain Image jed78 Wed, 29/07/2026 - 12:26 Author: Chika Tonooka Publisher: Princeton University Press Date published: 1 December 2026 (UK) Most historians of 19th and 20th-century Europe point to the persistence of racialised and hierarchical views of non-Europeans as "uncivilised." Yet these accounts overlook the profound intellectual impact of what contemporaries called the "awakening of Asia." In Rival Civilisations , Chika Tonooka shows how the rise of Japan after 1905 compelled British intellectuals to rethink…
